<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Han (206 BC)</h1><p class="st-meta">206 BCE – 202 BCE · capital Nanzheng</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The remote kingdom Xiang Yu gave Liu Bang in 206 BCE, from which Liu fought his way out to defeat Xiang Yu and found the Han dynasty.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>, a minor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> official turned rebel, was first to enter the Qin heartland and accepted the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziying">Ziying</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>, wary of him, made him King of Han in 206 BCE, ruling the isolated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanzhong">Hanzhong</a>, Ba and Shu regions from Nanzheng. Liu Bang burned the plank roads behind him to show he had no ambitions.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>With the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-he">Xiao He</a> managing supplies and the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xin">Han Xin</a> commanding the army, the kingdom became a base for war. Xiao He kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> records and grain stores, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan's</a> resources fed the campaigns.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-qins">Three Qins</a>, then fought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-chu">Western Chu</a> for four years, losing at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuzhou">Pengcheng</a> but recovering. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu's</a> death at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaixia">Gaixia</a> in 202 BCE, Liu Bang took the title of emperor, and his kingdom gave its name to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> and to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 206 BCE – 202 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.60%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>206 BCE – 202 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nanzheng</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Liu Bang</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese ancestral religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Han (Liu Bang), Hanzhong Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-204&amp;focus=kingdom-of-han-206-bc" aria-label="Kingdom of Han (206 BC) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7419 979 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Han (206 BC) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7739 1235L7909 1324M7739 1235L7769 1191M7739 1235L7948 1360M7739 1235L7769 1191M7739 1235L7855 1179M7739 1235L7885 1147M7739 1235L7925 1091"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7909 1324h0M7769 1191h0M7948 1360h0M7769 1191h0M7855 1179h0M7885 1147h0M7925 1091h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7739 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7739 1235h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nanzheng. <a href="/atlas?year=-204&amp;focus=kingdom-of-han-206-bc">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
